The other day I finished a game that had remained dormant on NAO for
several months. I was riding a ki-rin, and on Astral got zapped with a
wand of death. My steed was hit, but revived with an amulet of life
saving. I was still mounted, but from that point on continually got
the message "Placing steed onto map - Program in disorder, perhaps you
better #quit". Having invested well over 100K turns in this game
(initially an extinctionist attempt, until I inevitably got bored,
hence the long layoff), I did not intend to #quit, nor save or
otherwise interrupt the game, until I offered the Amulet.

In any case, I noticed that after this mishap, whenever I put on a
ring of conflict, my ki-rin started summoning nasties, which was
highly annoying as it impeded my progress. I don't remember this
happening before when I ascended riding a ki-rin, and I generally use
conflict continually on Astral. Also, at the end, my steed was not
listed next to my other pets on the "went to your reward" line. Which
prompts me to wonder - is it possible that my steed became untame once
life-saved (as sometimes happens), but still permitted me to ride
him?

I did Google the error message and found there is a known bug in 3.4.3
that things get wonky if a steed is life-saved after being hit with a
disintegration beam, so I expect the same might apply to a wand or
spell of death. Still, I am glad I was able to finish and ascend my
game despite the annoying error messages...


